# Example environment file for the systemd unit at contrib/automaton.service.
#
# Install:
#   sudo install -m 0600 -o root -g root \
#     automaton.env.example /etc/automaton.env
#   sudo vim /etc/automaton.env         # fill in AUTOMATON_PASSWORD
#   sudo systemctl daemon-reload
#   sudo systemctl enable --now automaton
#
# Mode 0600 / root-owned is intentional: AUTOMATON_PASSWORD is the
# encryption key for your on-disk wallet. Anyone who reads this file
# can unlock the keystore.

# REQUIRED — the passphrase that encrypts ~/.titon/automaton/wallet.enc.
# Set this to whatever you chose during `automaton init`. An EMPTY value
# is treated as "unset" (wallet/prompt.ts falls through to interactive
# input) — under systemd with no TTY, that path throws `NotInteractiveError`
# and the daemon fails to start. Check the failure via
# `journalctl -u automaton -n 50`.
AUTOMATON_PASSWORD=

# OPTIONAL — per-run overrides. Each of these also exists in config.json;
# the env var wins at runtime.
# AUTOMATON_NETWORK=testnet
# AUTOMATON_LOG_LEVEL=info
# AUTOMATON_METRICS_PORT=9090
